Dream League Application

Product Requirements & Technical Specification

Version 1.0

1. Purpose

The Dream League Application is a web application designed to replace the existing Excel-based management of the Dream League competition.

The Dream League has operated for over fifteen years and consists of a league competition and knockout cup competition based on goals scored by real-life football players.

The application should preserve the existing structure, rules and history of the competition whilst improving accessibility, administration and historical record keeping.

2. Competition Overview

League Structure

14 teams compete in the Dream League.
Teams are managed by one or more managers.
Teams compete across an entire football season.
League standings are determined by goals scored and goals conceded.
Cup Structure

A knockout cup competition runs during the spring.
Matches take place over designated cup weekends.
Winners progress to the next round.
Draws result in replays the following weekend.
